{"action_id":null,"arguments":[],"assumptions":[{"assumption_id":"node.265f351a2fec57605a484f64.a0","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Assess one identified benefit offered by one actor in one promotion to one client; assess distinct benefits separately.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.265f351a2fec57605a484f64.a1","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The actor is assessed using u1’s distributor definition. Coverage of persons who do not distribute SFC-authorised funds is unresolved.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.265f351a2fec57605a484f64.a2","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"A qualifying discount excludes that benefit only. A separate non-discount gift in the same promotion remains independently assessable.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.265f351a2fec57605a484f64.a3","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Actual investor distraction is the stated rationale, not an additional factual prerequisite.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.265f351a2fec57605a484f64.a4","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The formalization is a conditional reading of the retained standard; it does not establish temporal applicability or resolve missing authorities.","status":"PROVISIONAL"}],"bundle_hash":"555b5e195340bc01e00206c1710938e0825bc0ce647e5b64e549865000b8908c","candidate_id":"candidate.b156638fa54d43848fae18e328bf51bf","controlled_language":"Selected control: paragraph-10 gift-offer restriction, general-product reading. For an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds, if the intermediary offers a client a benefit that qualifies as a gift, the benefit is not a discount of fees or charges, and its offer promotes a specific investment product or a particular investment-product type, the offer departs from the stated should-not-offer standard. A product-type connection includes the specified fund-category and fund-house connections. Structured-product status and proof of actual distraction are not prerequisites. Within scope, a true formal result flags that departure; a false result addresses only this selected benefit and control.","disposition_reason":"Unreviewed interpretation proposal","family_ids":["scope"],"generation_phase":"BLIND_INITIAL","issue_ids":["issue.92256aa671f84b1e9a329e28fdcad6f9","issue.d731065e50a14b6fba6aeca246493a1a","issue.83502aca463946c7b3a2098ad9f1412b","issue.7a7ba4f331c643e6804c4b60c77ac455","issue.42a6e70eda854fb198c152e5c4730ca7"],"parent_id":null,"probability_of_legal_correctness":null,"revision_reason":"R1 gives operative weight to u14’s generic investment-product wording. For a distributor within u1, an otherwise qualifying gift linked to a non-fund investment product is within this selected reading. R2 excludes that case from its scope. The strongest uncertainty is whether the circular is restating the Code’s general reach or only describing its fund-specific application.","run_id":"run.43cfe1f6c26f47b89fa28eb53ba97027","scheduling_priority":0,"schema_version":"interpretation.v1","score_purpose":"INVESTIGATION_PRIORITY_ONLY","source_packet_hash":"7b78bffd5267abb04c58ab204d1e34f621dc3fb03008be1b35980abcaa535ba4","source_unit_ids":["u1","u13","u14","u29"],"status":"ACTIVE","subject_unit":"Paragraph-10 gift-promotion control"}